{"kind": "instructions", "path": "AGENTS.md", "text": "# Trillionnium Chain development boundary\n\nBefore edits, builds, commits or pushes, run `bash scripts/project-preflight.sh`.\nThe sole plan is `docs/development/TRNM_AI_NATIVE_BLOCKCHAIN_DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md`.\nActual M00-M17 source ownership is in `config/portability-inventory-v1.json`.\nPreserve concurrent changes and use the existing integration candidate into main.\n\nOnly reusable candidate components remain. Do not restore retired consensus code,\nprotocol trees, deployment jobs or legacy appendices. Git history is the archive.\nDo not create a successful stub or a silent fallback to disguise an unimplemented\nwork primitive, consensus runtime, reorganization layer or model product loop.\n\nChanged signed domains and stored schemas require fresh namespaces and exact tests.\nLocal operation and revocation history must not rewind with chain reorganization.\nDeployed data, keys, running services and other repositories are outside this scope.\nNo force push, self-approval, protected-main bypass or activation is permitted here.\n\nVerify the exact Cargo graph, lockfile, retained tests, strict Clippy and formatting,\nnegative source-integrity tests and Markdown links on the exact committed source.\nPreserve failed observations; source checks do not certify model efficacy or release.\n"}
{"kind": "instructions", "path": "PROJECT_BOUNDARY.md", "text": "# Project boundary\n\nRepository: TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain. Lane: chain-consensus.\nTarget: pon-nakamoto-v1. Implementation: portable foundations only; no activated node.\n\nThe JSON policy binds canonical origin, existing review requirements, development branches,\nactual workspace and prohibition on cross-repository path dependencies. Git is the archive.\nDeployed data, keys, running services and other repositories are outside this cleanup.\n"}
{"kind": "instructions", "path": "OPERATIONS.md", "text": "# Operating scope\n\nThis repository does not install or activate a public consensus node. Use a fresh revision2\nnamespace for local experiments; old SQLite schemas and old genesis context are rejected.\nDo not point candidate programs at deployed databases, secrets or real signing identities.\n\nThe reference Ledger can explicitly select the native M06 application through\n`TRNM_NATIVE_EXECUTOR=/absolute/path/to/release/examples/pon_execute` and\n`TRNM_EXECUTION_WORKERS=1|2|4|8`. Missing or mismatched binaries fail; reference fallback is\nnot automatic. Startup recovers its own initialization/reorg intent and best verified tip.\nThe subprocess bridge is a tested integration boundary, not a persistent production host.\n\nRun `bash scripts/ci/ci_job.sh protocol-contract` after building prerequisites. The full\nRust lane uses locked dependencies, tests and strict Clippy. Preserve raw failure results\nand declare filesystem and backend. Localhost experiments and public fixture keys never\nbecome independent operators, physical durability or real Hepta user-task evidence.\n"}
